From 3d91ef799da784ddb8e39f47c543282e00d15c71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 05:14:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 036/147] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8350: Fix the IPA interrupt

The IPA interrupt of SM8350 is SPI 654, as in the vendor device tree of
the SoC ("ipa-irq", 0x28e) and as on SC7280 and SM8550, not 655. With
the wrong line the AP never sees an IPA interrupt: /proc/interrupts
counts 0 on every CPU, the microcontroller's INIT_COMPLETED response is
never handled, so the IPA keeps the proxy power reference taken for the
microcontroller forever (it never runtime-suspends), and a modem that is
restarted after it had booted once (a stop and start, or the recovery
after a crash) asserts 3.4 seconds later: "ipa_hwp_init.c:420:IPA Assert:
0 failed: ipa_hwp_init_rsp_timer_cb: didnt rx any ind frm HWP", and keeps
doing so at every recovery.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
index fed3b83468ef..7d4c13f7aef5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8350.dtsi
@@ -1846,7 +1846,7 @@ ipa: ipa@1e40000 {
 				    "ipa-shared",
 				    "gsi";
 
-			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 655 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
+			interrupts-extended = <&intc GIC_SPI 654 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 					      <&intc GIC_SPI 432 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
 					      <&ipa_smp2p_in 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>,
 					      <&ipa_smp2p_in 1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
